{"pageProps": {"params": {"versionId": "59", "usfm": "JOS.12.ESV"}, "audioVersionInfo": {"title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "copyright_long": {"text": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament", "html": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament"}, "copyright_short": {"text": "\u2117 2016 Crossway", "html": "<p>\u2117 2016 Crossway</p>"}, "version_id": 59, "id": 1, "publisher_link": "", "dramatized": false, "publisher": {"id": 575, "name": "Hear Book Audio", "local_name": "Hear Book Audio", "url": null, "description": null}}, "type": "chapter", "chapterInfo": {"audioChapterInfo": [{"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1/32k/JOS/12-d982281816e48a8e830359c0c44f83cc.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1/m4a/32k/JOS/12-d982281816e48a8e830359c0c44f83cc.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1, "version_id": 59, "title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "timing_available": true, "dramatized": false, "default": true}], "content": "<div class=\"version vid59 iso6393eng\" data-vid=\"59\" data-iso6393=\"eng\">\n    <div class=\"book bkJOS\">\n        <div class=\"chapter ch12\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12\">\n            <div class=\"label\">12</div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">Kings Defeated by Moses</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"verse v1\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.1\"><span class=\"label\">1</span><span class=\"content\">Now these are the kings of the land whom the people of Israel defeated and took possession of their land beyond the Jordan toward the sunrise, from </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Num. 21:13, 24; Deut. 3:8, 9 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the Valley of the Arnon to Mount Hermon, with all </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Deut. 1:1</span></span><span class=\"content\">the Arabah eastward: </span></span><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.2\"><span class=\"label\">2</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Deut. 2:32, 33; 3:6, 16; See Num. 21:21-26 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Sihon king of the Amorites who lived at Heshbon and ruled from Aroer, which is on the edge of the Valley of the Arnon, and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Deut. 2:36 </span></span><span class=\"content\">from the middle of the valley as far as the </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Gen. 32:22</span></span><span class=\"content\">river Jabbok, the boundary of the Ammonites, that is, half of Gilead, </span></span><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.3\"><span class=\"label\">3</span><span class=\"content\">and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 1 above] </span></span><span class=\"content\">the Arabah </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 11:2 </span></span><span class=\"content\">to the Sea of Chinneroth eastward, and in the direction of Beth-jeshimoth, to the Sea of the Arabah, the Salt Sea, southward to the foot of </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 13:20; Deut. 3:17; 4:49</span></span><span class=\"content\">the slopes of Pisgah; </span></span><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.4\"><span class=\"label\">4</span><span class=\"content\">and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Deut. 3:3, 10; See Num. 21:33-35 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Og</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">12:4 </span><span class=\"ft\">Septuagint; Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">the boundary of Og</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> king of Bashan, one of the remnant of </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 13:12; 15:8; 18:16 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the Rephaim, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 9:10; Deut. 1:4</span></span><span class=\"content\">who lived at Ashtaroth and at Edrei </span></span><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.5\"><span class=\"label\">5</span><span class=\"content\">and ruled over </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Deut. 3:8, 9 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Mount Hermon and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 13:11; Deut. 3:10 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Salecah and all Bashan </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Deut. 3:14</span></span><span class=\"content\">to the boundary of the Geshurites and the Maacathites, and over half of Gilead to the boundary of Sihon king of Heshbon. </span></span><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.6\"><span class=\"label\">6</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Num. 21:23, 24, 33-35 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Moses, the servant of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">, and the people of Israel defeated them. And Moses the servant of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 13:8; Num. 32:29, 33; Deut. 3:11, 12</span></span><span class=\"content\">gave their land for a possession to the Reubenites and the Gadites and the half-tribe of Manasseh.</span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">Kings Defeated by Joshua</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.6\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.7\"><span class=\"label\">7</span><span class=\"content\">And these are the kings of the land whom Joshua and the people of Israel defeated on the west side of the Jordan, from Baal-gad in the Valley of Lebanon to </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 11:17 </span></span><span class=\"content\">Mount Halak, that rises toward Seir (and Joshua gave their land to the tribes of Israel as a possession </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 11:23; 18:10</span></span><span class=\"content\">according to their allotments, </span></span><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.8\"><span class=\"label\">8</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 10:40; 11:16 </span></span><span class=\"content\">in the hill country, in the lowland, in the Arabah, in the slopes, in the wilderness, and in the Negeb, the land of </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 9:1</span></span><span class=\"content\">the Hittites, the Amorites, the Canaanites, the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites): </span></span><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.9\"><span class=\"label\">9</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 6:2] </span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Jericho, one; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 8:29</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Ai, which is beside Bethel, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.10\"><span class=\"label\">10</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 10:23</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Jerusalem, one; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 10:23</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Hebron, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.11\"><span class=\"label\">11</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 10 above]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Jarmuth, one; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 10 above]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Lachish, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.12\"><span class=\"label\">12</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 10 above] </span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Eglon, one; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 10:33</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Gezer, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.13\"><span class=\"label\">13</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 10:38, 39</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Debir, one; the king of Geder, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.14\"><span class=\"label\">14</span><span class=\"content\">the king of Hormah, one; the king of Arad, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.15\"><span class=\"label\">15</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 10:29</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Libnah, one; the king of Adullam, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.16\"><span class=\"label\">16</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 10:28 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Makkedah, one; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 8:17; Judg. 1:22</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Bethel, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.17\"><span class=\"label\">17</span><span class=\"content\">the king of Tappuah, one; the king of Hepher, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.18\"><span class=\"label\">18</span><span class=\"content\">the king of Aphek, one; the king of Lasharon, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.19\"><span class=\"label\">19</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 11:1 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Madon, one; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 11:1, 10</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Hazor, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v20\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.20\"><span class=\"label\">20</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 19 above]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Shimron-meron, one; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 19 above]</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Achshaph, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v21\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.21\"><span class=\"label\">21</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 17:11</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Taanach, one; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 17:11</span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Megiddo, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.22\"><span class=\"label\">22</span><span class=\"content\">the king of Kedesh, one; the king of Jokneam in Carmel, one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v23\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.23\"><span class=\"label\">23</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 21 above] </span></span><span class=\"content\">the king of Dor in </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 11:2</span></span><span class=\"content\">Naphath-dor, one; the king of Goiim in Galilee,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">12:23 </span><span class=\"ft\">Septuagint; Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">Gilgal</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> one; </span></span><span class=\"verse v24\" data-usfm=\"JOS.12.24\"><span class=\"label\">24</span><span class=\"content\">the king of Tirzah, one: in all, thirty-one kings.</span></span></div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>", "copyright": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers."}, "next": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["JOS.13"], "human": "Joshua 13", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "previous": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["JOS.11"], "human": "Joshua 11", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "reference": {"usfm": ["JOS.12"], "human": "Joshua 12", "version_id": 59}}, "usfm": "JOS.12.ESV", "locale": "en", "versionData": {"audio": true, "copyright_short": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers."}, "id": 59, "language": {"iso_639_1": "en", "iso_639_3": "eng", "language_tag": "eng", "local_name": "English", "text_direction": "ltr"}, "local_abbreviation": "ESV", "local_title": "English Standard Version 2016", "publisher": {"name": "Crossway / Good News Publishers"}, "reader_footer": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers